James inquired about dynamically updating a `leaflet` map's underlying shapefile in a Shiny application. I provided guidance on several aspects, including checking the console for errors, ensuring reactivity, debugging strategies, and sample code. I highlighted the importance of using `observe` to run side-effect code in a reactive context, allowing the app to track changes and manage dependencies effectively. This protects against issues during updates and ensures that the shapefile can be loaded and displayed correctly when user inputs change.
